 "notes": [
  "Selectivity (compound split): ranking a compound's top-decile lines, PR-AUC 0.238 (95% CI lower 0.221) vs cell-line-mean 0.192 \u2014 **better**. Ordering the full list of lines, per-compound \u03c1 0.270 (CI lower 0.254) vs 0.275 \u2014 not better. The compound-only ablation scores 0.101 on that PR-AUC, at the 0.100 prevalence floor, because it cannot vary across lines: the model's margin therefore comes from the cell-line expression features. **The model identifies which lines respond most to a given compound better than the line-average ranking does, but does not order the full list better.** Read the top of the list as the usable signal, not the tail.",
  "Headline set (D-03): 467,725 rows, 938 compounds, 977 cell lines.",
  "Regression target: DSS3 percentile under the training distribution (D-04). The within_top10 AUCs use the dedicated classifier's probability; all other metrics use the regressor.",
  "per-cell-line \u03c1 ranks compounds within a line (potency); per-compound \u03c1 ranks lines within a compound (selectivity).",
  "compound_only cannot vary across lines, so its per-compound \u03c1 is undefined: it isolates potency.",
  "CIs: 95% percentile bootstrap over test compounds (200 resamples).",
  "Mixed-scale sensitivity analysis (D-03; 20 compounds added with DSS3 \u2265 1 \u00d7 0.01, 484,733 rows, compound split, no CI): per-cell-line \u03c1 0.375, per-compound \u03c1 0.318, within_top10 PR-AUC 0.236."
 ],
